			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Pathfinder Companion: Dwarves of Golarion, Front Inside Cover</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Detect Alignment (Sp)</name>
			<description>At will, an inquisitor can use detect chaos, detect evil, detect good, or detect law. She can only use one of these at any given time.</description>
			<type>INQUISITORCLASSFEATURES.SPECIALQUALITY.SPELLLIKE</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Player&#39;s Guide, p.40</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Discern Lies (Sp)</name>
			<description>An inquisitor can discern lies, as per the spell, for 5 rounds per day. These rounds do not need to be consecutive. Activating this ability is an immediate action.</description>
			<type>INQUISITORCLASSFEATURES.SPECIALQUALITY.SPELLLIKE</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Player&#39;s Guide, p.41</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Greed</name>
			<description>Dwarves receive a +2 racial bonus on Appraise skill checks made to determine the price of nonmagical goods that contain precious metals or gemstones.</description>
			<type>RACIALTRAITS.DWARF RACIAL TRAIT.DWARF RACIAL DEFAULT.SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Pathfinder Companion: Dwarves of Golarion, Front Inside Cover</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Hardy</name>
			<description>Dwarves receive a +2 racial bonus on saving throws against poison, spells, and spell-like abilities.</description>
			<type>RACIALTRAITS.DWARF RACIAL TRAIT.DWARF RACIAL DEFAULT.SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>SaveBonus: +2 racial bonus on saving throws against poison, spells, and spell-like abilities.</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Pathfinder Companion: Dwarves of Golarion, Front Inside Cover</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Judgment (Profane) (Su)</name>
			<description>An inquisitor can pronounce judgment upon her foes as a swift action. Starting when the judgment is made, the inquisitor receives a bonus or special ability based on the type of judgment made. An inquisitor can use this ability 2 times per day. Once activated, this ability lasts until the combat ends, at which point all of the bonuses immediately end. The inquisitor must participate in the combat to gain these bonuses. If she is frightened, panicked, paralyzed, stunned, unconscious, or otherwise prevented from participating in the combat, the ability does not end, but the bonuses do not resume until she can participate in the combat again. When the inquisitor uses this ability, she must select one type of judgment to make. As a swift action, she can change this judgment to another type.</description>
			<type>INQUISITORCLASSFEATURES.SPECIALQUALITY.SUPERNATURAL.INQUISITORJUDGMENT</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Player&#39;s Guide, p.38</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Monster Lore (Ex)</name>
			<description>The inquisitor adds her Wisdom modifier on Knowledge skill checks in addition to her Intelligence modifier, when making skill checks to identify the abilities and weaknesses of creatures.</description>
			<type>INQUISITORCLASSFEATURES.SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Player&#39;s Guide, p.40</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Solo Tactics (Ex)</name>
			<description>All of the inquisitor&#39;s allies are treated as if they possessed the same teamwork feats as the inquisitor for the purpose of determining whether the inquisitor receives a bonus from her teamwork feats. Her allies do not receive any bonuses from these feats unless they actually possess the feats themselves. The allies&#39; positioning and actions must still meet the prerequisites listed in the teamwork feat for the inquisitor to receive the listed bonus.</description>
			<type>INQUISITORCLASSFEATURES.SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Player&#39;s Guide, p.40</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Stability</name>
			<description>Dwarves receive a +4 racial bonus to their Combat Maneuver Defense when resisting a bull rush or trip attempt while standing on the ground.</description>
			<type>RACIALTRAITS.DWARF RACIAL TRAIT.DWARF RACIAL DEFAULT.SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>CombatBonus: +4 bonus to their Combat Maneuver Defense when resisting a bull rush or trip attempt while standing on the ground.</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Pathfinder Companion: Dwarves of Golarion, Front Inside Cover</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Stonecunning</name>
			<description>Dwarves receive a +2 bonus on Perception checks to potentially notice unusual stonework, such as traps and hidden doors located in stone walls or floors. They receive a check to notice such features whenever they pass within 10 feet of them, whether or not they are actively looking.</description>
			<type>RACIALTRAITS.DWARF RACIAL TRAIT.DWARF RACIAL DEFAULT.SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>SkillBonus: +2 bonus on Perception skill checks to notice unusual stonework, such as traps and hidden doors located in stone walls or floors.</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Pathfinder Companion: Dwarves of Golarion, Front Inside Cover</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Track (Ex)</name>
			<description>An inquisitor adds half her level on Survival skill checks made to follow or identify tracks.</description>
			<type>INQUISITORCLASSFEATURES.SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Player&#39;s Guide, p.40</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Weapon Familiarity</name>
			<description>Dwarves are proficient with battleaxes, heavy picks, and warhammers, and treat any weapon with the word &quot;dwarven&quot; in its name as a martial weapon.</description>
			<type>RACIALTRAITS.DWARF RACIAL TRAIT.DWARF RACIAL DEFAULT.SPECIALQUALITY.WEAPON FAMILIARITY.RACIALWEAPONFAMILIARITY</type>
